{title: I Am the Resurrection}
{subtitle: John 11:25–26}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Gm] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Four days he lay in the [F/A]Bethany tomb
[Gm7]The mourners wept in every [Eb]room
[Bb]Martha ran out [F/A]to meet him on the road
[Gm7]Carrying a sorrow too [Eb]heavy to hold
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[Cm7]Lord, if you had been here, [Gm7]my brother would not have died
Your [Ab]brother will rise a[F]gain
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]I am the resurrection [F/A]and the life
Who[Gm7]ever believes in me will [Eb]live, even though he [Bb]dies
Everyone who lives and believes [F/A]in me will never die
Do you [Gm7]be[Eb]lieve [F][Bb]this? [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]He came up to the cave with the [F/A]stone laid across
And [Gm7]Jesus wept beside them [Eb]as they grieved for their loss
[Bb]Then he lifted up his eyes and he [F/A]thanked the Father there
And [Gm7]his voice like thunder went [Eb]ringing through the air
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Cm7]Lazarus, come out!
Un[Gm]bind him and let him go
[Ab]Yes, Lord. I believe [F]that you are the Christ
The Son of [Bb]God
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I am the resurrec[F/A]tion and the [Gm7]life
Whoever believes in me [Eb]will live, even though [Bb]he dies
Everyone who lives and believes [F/A]in me will never die
Do [Gm7]you [Eb]believe [F][Bb][F/A]this?
{end_of_chorus}

